n": "(Green, Ohio: Brian Williams) The Republican Party's spending on clothing for Governor Sarah Palin and her family and the Republican lag in the polls noted. [PALIN \u2013 reacts to requests to release her medical records.] Earlier interview held with Senator John McCain and Palin. [McCAIN \u2013 says he\u2019s always done best when he\u2019s a little behind; says he respects Senator Barack Obama but there are differences; responds to remarks from Senators Joe Biden and Joe Lieberman about new presidents being tested; comments on Lieberman crossing party lines to support him.] [PALIN \u2013 states her view on preconditions for talking to dictators; comments on Biden\u2019s remarks.] Former Secretary of State Colin Powell\u2019s endorsement of Obama and his statement that Palin is not qualified to be president noted. [McCAIN \u2013 defends Palin; outlines her record.] [PALIN \u2013 says she has more executive experience than Obama; notes McCain has gotten endorsements from 5 former Secretaries of State, military brass and those who are more economic-minded.]  \n\n(Green, Ohio: Brian Williams) Obama\u2019s response to Biden\u2019s comments about being tested like President John F. Kennedy noted; scenes shown from Richmond, Virginia. [OBAMA \u2013 says Joe engages in rhetorical flourishes but his point was that the next administration will be tested regardless of who it is.] ", "segment_duration": 760, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63070.0", "legacy_segment_id": 921828, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "LuBtgN4e88", "broadcast_date": "2008-10-22", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1730, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadca